# The Lune that zn embeds, one pinned entry per platform (f0427). Lune 0.10.5, from github.com/lune-org/lune.
# Line: <kind> <platform> <sha256> <name>. A zip entry pins the release zip; a bin entry pins the binary itself.
# How each pin was taken, plainly:
#   linux-x86_64 (zip): the sha256 of the release zip lune-0.10.5-linux-x86_64.zip, recorded by experiment E5 of f0427
#     (gh release view v0.10.5, then a download) on 2026-11-21.
#   darwin-aarch64 (bin): trust on first use. It is the sha256 of the copy rokit had installed on this machine since
#     2026-10-16, measured on 2026-11-21 and NOT compared with any published value.
# z-nile/lib/znbuild.sh (through cmd/znpack) refuses a Lune whose digest differs. The other platforms are pinned with the
# release packaging (f0427 step 12), where every pin becomes a zip pin taken from the published release.
zip linux-x86_64 1fb5dee6a1afa1d300092805c6e660fe06144d29dd68c45cf6956f040667f791 lune-0.10.5-linux-x86_64.zip
bin darwin-aarch64 e4cc1b42a45e5f6fbb9a3b66931f61a9864b540861d98c0b3fdae2cfd374fd4e lune
